        <mxCell id="38H596Q46nBDXimof066-206" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;ASSUMPTIONS&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;&quot;&gt;* All customer car parking data is &quot;clean&quot; (can&#39;t just drive in/out over a kerb, customers swap a trailer inside car park, etc).&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;&quot;&gt;* All VRN lookups are successful (no foreign vehicles, VRN reading issues).&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;&quot;&gt;* Idempotency throughout (particularly&amp;nbsp;queue consumers).&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;&quot;&gt;* External data access locked down to the API with all correct Authentication, Authorisation, multi-tenant separation.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;&quot;&gt;* All Azure hosted.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;&quot;&gt;* I&#39;m not sure Visit Logic Rules to determine how&lt;span style=&quot;text-align: center; background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;Azure Event Hub telemetry should be interpreted need to be in a DB&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; and not embedded within the service, depending upon how changeable or individualised these are.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-align: center; background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;* Overstay Logic Rules are specific to each car park, tenant, times, VRN&#39;s and regularly changeable.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-align: center; background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;* Each carpark has only 1 set of rules applied across all spaces:&lt;br&gt;&lt;i&gt;&amp;nbsp; (ignores electric charging, disabled spaces, parent spaces, poor parking,&amp;nbsp;reserved spaces)&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="168.75" width="680" x="-1374" y="378" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
